  "verdict": "**ARGMAX IS NOT SYSTEMATICALLY BETTER, AND NOW THERE IS A CONTROL TO SAY SO.** Conditional on arrival at the 30 eligible start states, argmax clears pipe 2 at 3-40% across 4 checkpoints (Wilson ~\u00b118 pp at n=30) \u2014 a spread far wider than the interval, so the variation is between checkpoints, not noise. Against **sampling from the identical start states**, argmax wins pipe 2 on 0 of 4 checkpoints (deltas [-36.7, -66.7, -43.3, -43.3] pp). **Block 54's x=916 was one trajectory from one checkpoint, and on a proper multi-start basis determinism carries no consistent advantage.** These numbers are conditional-on-arrival and must never be placed beside an n=200 single-life figure.",
